At t=0 a resolver caches app.example A 192.0.2.10 with TTL 300, and missing.example NXDOMAIN with negative TTL 60. At t=20 authoritative app A changes to 192.0.2.20. Fresh positive answers retain the original TTL. Assume authoritative queries complete instantly. No proactive refresh or serve-stale. Query app at t=300, and missing at t=61. Return app address, remaining TTL, whether missing requires authoritative lookup, and earliest t at which app requires fresh resolution. Expiration is t >= original TTL.

Required output schema (type descriptions, not answer values): {"address":"IPv4 string","remaining_ttl":"integer seconds","negative_lookup":"boolean","refresh_at":"integer seconds"}

